# Python Pre-commit Hooks

## Requirement

All Python projects SHALL use pre-commit hooks to enforce code quality before commits.

### Required Hooks

- SHALL include ruff for linting and formatting
- SHALL include mypy for type checking
- SHALL include pytest for running tests
- SHALL include secret scanning (detect-secrets)
- SHALL include other project-specific hooks as needed

### Pre-commit Configuration

- Projects SHALL include `.pre-commit-config.yaml` file
- Pre-commit hooks SHALL be installed via `pre-commit install`
- Pre-commit hooks SHALL run automatically on `git commit`
- Pre-commit hooks SHALL be runnable manually via `pre-commit run --all-files`

### CI/CD Integration

- Pre-commit hooks SHALL also run in CI/CD pipelines
- CI/CD SHALL use the same hooks as local development
- Failed hooks SHALL fail the CI/CD pipeline

## Rationale

Using pre-commit hooks provides:

- **Quality**: Catches issues before they enter the repository
- **Consistency**: Ensures all commits meet quality standards
- **Efficiency**: Fixes issues early, before code review
- **Standards**: Enforces coding standards automatically
- **Security**: Scans for accidentally committed secrets
- **Team Alignment**: All team members use the same checks

## Implementation

### .pre-commit-config.yaml

```yaml
repos:
  # Ruff for linting and formatting
  - repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit
    rev: v0.1.0
    hooks:
      - id: ruff
        args: [--fix, --exit-non-zero-on-fix]
      - id: ruff-format

  # MyPy for type checking
  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-mypy
    rev: v1.7.0
    hooks:
      - id: mypy
        additional_dependencies: [types-all]

  # Pytest for tests
  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: pytest
        name: pytest
        entry: pytest
        language: system
        types: [python]
        pass_filenames: false
        always_run: true

  # Secret scanning
  - repo: https://github.com/Yelp/detect-secrets
    rev: v1.4.0
    hooks:
      - id: detect-secrets
        args: ['--baseline', '.secrets.baseline']

  # General file checks
  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/pre-commit-hooks
    rev: v4.5.0
    hooks:
      - id: trailing-whitespace
      - id: end-of-file-fixer
      - id: check-yaml
      - id: check-added-large-files
      - id: check-json
      - id: check-toml
```

### Installing Pre-commit

```bash
# Install pre-commit
pip install pre-commit

# Install git hooks
pre-commit install

# Run on all files (first time)
pre-commit run --all-files
```

### Makefile Integration

```makefile
.PHONY: pre-commit-install
pre-commit-install:
	pre-commit install

.PHONY: pre-commit
pre-commit:
	pre-commit run --all-files

.PHONY: pre-commit-update
pre-commit-update:
	pre-commit autoupdate
```

### CI/CD Integration

```yaml
# .github/workflows/pre-commit.yml
name: Pre-commit

on: [push, pull_request]

jobs:
  pre-commit:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v4
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'
      - name: Install pre-commit
        run: pip install pre-commit
      - name: Run pre-commit
        run: pre-commit run --all-files
```

### Custom Local Hooks

```yaml
# .pre-commit-config.yaml
repos:
  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: custom-check
        name: Custom Check
        entry: bash -c 'python scripts/custom_check.py'
        language: system
        types: [python]
```

### Bypassing Pre-commit (When Necessary)

```bash
# Skip pre-commit hooks (use sparingly)
git commit --no-verify -m "Emergency fix"

# Run specific hook
pre-commit run ruff --all-files
```

## Integration

This rule works in conjunction with:

- `python/ruff-check-format.mdc` - Ruff linting and formatting
- `python/typing.mdc` - MyPy type checking
- `python/testing-framework.mdc` - Pytest for tests
- `python/secrets-management.mdc` - Secret scanning
